//
// This used to happen whenever VITE_SUPABASE_URL / VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
// weren't set at build time — which turned out to be inconsistent across every
// place this project actually runs: Lovable's own hosting injects them
// automatically, but a local `npm run dev` needs a `.env` Vite picks up at
// *startup* (a stale running dev server or cache won't see a newly-added one),
// and Vercel/Netlify/Cloudflare Pages need them set in that host's own
// dashboard before a build, not read from anything shipped in the repo/zip.
// Three different platforms, three different places to configure the same
// two values — too easy for one of them to be missing.
//
// Real fix: stop depending on env vars being configured at all. The anon/
// publishable key below is meant to be public in a client bundle by design —
// it's not the service_role key, and this project's Row Level Security
// policies are what actually protect data, the same way they would if this
// value were read from an env var instead. So it's hardcoded as the default,
// with env vars only as an *override* (e.g. pointing a build at a different
// Supabase project later) rather than a requirement. This makes the app work
// out of the box on Lovable, Vercel, and local — no platform-specific setup
// step required — while still respecting VITE_SUPABASE_URL /
